<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Analyzing Independence: Assessing the Relationship Between Events A and B</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>If \(P[A]={@p_a@},P[B]={@p_b@}\) and \(P[A \cup B]={@p_aub@}\), are events \(A\) and \(B\) independent?</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>If two events \(A\) and \(B\) are independent, then we must have \(P[A \cap B] = P[A] \times P[B]\). However,</p>
<p>\(P[A \cap B]=P[A]+P[B]-P[A \cup B]={@p_a@}+{@p_b@}-{@p_aub@}={@decimalplaces((p_a+p_b-p_aub),2)@}\)</p>
<p>\(P[A] \times P[B]={@p_a@} \times {@p_b@}={@decimalplaces(p_a*p_b,4)@} \neq P[A \cap B]\), therefore they cannot be independent.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
